Unreal Gold port: SDLDrv typed-key auto-repeat fix. Always on, in every mode.

Applies to SDLDrv/ from OldUnreal-UnrealPatch227k-SDK-Linux.tar.bz2
(v227k_15) with `patch -p1 -F0` run in the directory containing SDLDrv/,
after SDLDrv-handheld.patch (as build.sh does) or on its own. No class
layout changes: the new state lives in file statics.

SDLDrv emulates key repeat for typed characters itself, because SDL text
input is off. Stock UpdateInput set a 0.5 s delay on KEY_DOWN and, at the
end of the same call, subtracted DeltaSeconds, the time since the previous
UpdateInput. That time passed before the key went down. So whenever the
frame before a key press took longer than 0.5 s (a level load, a save, a
decode hitch, a slow renderer), a key that was only tapped was typed twice.
On the handheld that doubles a digit typed into a mod keypad or a UWindow
edit box.

Now:
- the repeat is timed in real time (appSeconds) from the UpdateInput that
  saw the key go down: first repeat after 0.5 s, then every 0.1 s, as before.
  A key pressed during a hitch thus gets its full 0.5 s once the game runs
  again, as the player saw no feedback during the hitch;
- the key must still be held according to SDL_GetKeyboardState, and only
  the viewport that saw it go down repeats it. Stock repeated a key forever
  when its KEY_UP went to another viewport's UpdateInput;
- one UpdateInput sends at most one repeat; after a long frame the cadence
  restarts instead of catching up.

New SDL import: SDL_GetKeyboardState, which the official libSDL3 and the
port's SDL3 shim both export.

--- a/SDLDrv/Src/SDLViewport.cpp
+++ b/SDLDrv/Src/SDLViewport.cpp
@@ -1528,6 +1528,17 @@
 }
 
 //
+// Typed-key auto-repeat state (see the end of UpdateInput): the viewport that saw
+// the key in its KeyRepeatKey go down, the key's scancode and the real time it went
+// down. File statics rather than USDLViewport members, so the class layout stays
+// that of the official SDLDrv.so. SDL has one keyboard and one event queue, drained
+// by whichever viewport's UpdateInput runs, so only one key auto-repeats at a time.
+//
+static USDLViewport* KeyRepeatViewport = NULL;
+static SDL_Scancode  KeyRepeatScancode = SDL_SCANCODE_UNKNOWN;
+static FTime         KeyRepeatDownTime;
+
+//
 // Update input for this viewport.
 //
 #if UNREAL_OLDUNREAL || UNREAL_TOURNAMENT_OLDUNREAL
@@ -1737,6 +1748,10 @@
 
 						// Initial delay before auto-repeat kicks in.
 						KeyRepeatTimer = 0.5f;
+						// ... counted in real time from now (see the auto-repeat at the end).
+						KeyRepeatViewport = this;
+						KeyRepeatScancode = Event.key.scancode;
+						KeyRepeatDownTime = appSeconds();
 
 						if (KeyRepeatKey != IK_None)
 							Client->Engine->Key(this, KeyRepeatKey
@@ -2170,17 +2185,42 @@
 	}
 
 	// stijn: Auto-repeat the last typed key at a fixed rate
+	//
+	// Port fix: time the repeat in real time from the UpdateInput that saw the key go
+	// down. Stock code subtracted DeltaSeconds here, right after a KEY_DOWN in this
+	// same call had set the 0.5 s delay. DeltaSeconds, the time since the previous
+	// UpdateInput, passed before the key went down, so one frame longer than 0.5 s (a
+	// level load, a save, a texture decode hitch) repeated a key that was only tapped:
+	// a digit typed into a mod keypad or a UWindow edit box came out twice. Now:
+	// - KeyRepeatTimer is how long after KeyRepeatDownTime the next repeat is due:
+	//   0.5 s, then every 0.1 s, as before;
+	// - only the viewport that saw the latest typed key go down repeats it, and only
+	//   while SDL's keyboard state says the key is still held. Its KEY_UP may never
+	//   reach this viewport (another viewport's UpdateInput drained it, or
+	//   UseHIDKeyboard skipped it), and stock then repeated the key forever;
+	// - one call sends at most one repeat; after a long frame the 0.1 s cadence
+	//   restarts instead of catching up.
 	if (KeyRepeatKey != IK_None)
 	{
-		KeyRepeatTimer -= DeltaSeconds;
-		if (KeyRepeatTimer <= 0.f)
+		INT         NumKeys  = 0;
+		const bool* KeyState = SDL_GetKeyboardState(&NumKeys);
+		if (KeyRepeatViewport != this || !KeyState || (INT)KeyRepeatScancode >= NumKeys || !KeyState[KeyRepeatScancode])
+		{
+			KeyRepeatKey     = IK_None;
+			KeyRepeatUnicode = 0;
+		}
+		else
 		{
-			KeyRepeatTimer = 0.1f; // Repeat rate once the initial delay has elapsed.
-			Client->Engine->Key(this, KeyRepeatKey
+			const FLOAT HeldSeconds = appSeconds() - KeyRepeatDownTime;
+			if (HeldSeconds >= KeyRepeatTimer)
+			{
+				KeyRepeatTimer = HeldSeconds + 0.1f; // Repeat rate once the initial delay has elapsed.
+				Client->Engine->Key(this, KeyRepeatKey
 #if !UNREAL_TOURNAMENT_OLDUNREAL
-				, KeyRepeatUnicode
+					, KeyRepeatUnicode
 #endif
-			);
+				);
+			}
 		}
 	}
 
